8.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains complete consensus on F (None of the above is correct). Across all three experiments, the data demonstrate that reverse transcription of transposable elements triggers innate immune sensing via STING and downstream type I interferon signaling (IFNAR1) to promote maternal erythropoiesis and progenitor expansion during pregnancy. Options A, B, E, G, and H directly contradict these experimental findings by denying the positive roles of interferon or immune activation, or by claiming interferon inhibitors cannot impair red blood cell levels. Furthermore, option D introduces an unsubstantiated insertional mutagenesis mechanism, and option C proposes an unfounded, genotoxically hazardous therapeutic extrapolation to treat anemia. Consequently, option F is the only valid choice.
}

