PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel is completely and unanimously unified behind Option F ("None of the above is correct"). The three experimental datasets define an integrated physiological cascade in pregnant mice: endogenous retrotransposon reverse transcription generates cytosolic cDNA sensed by cGAS-STING to stimulate type I interferon signaling (IFNAR1), promoting maternal erythropoiesis and splenic progenitor expansion. Distractors A, B, E, G, and H are factually contradicted by empirical loss-of-function phenotypes, D falsely posits genomic insertional mutagenesis into the Ifnar1 regulatory region, and C represents an ungrounded, clinically hazardous extrapolation.
}

